1. SUBJECT AND ACCEPTANCE

REFORMAMINI is a desktop application for Bible study, developed and published by
its author (the "Licensor").

This agreement governs the use of the REFORMAMINI program, including its executable
code, its original resources and its documentation (the "Software").

By installing, copying or using the Software you accept this agreement in full.
If you do not accept it, do not install or use the Software.

Each version of the Software is delivered with the version of this agreement
in force at the time of its publication, which governs the use of that
version of the Software. Installing a later version implies accepting the
agreement that accompanies it.

2. GRANT OF USE

The Licensor grants you a free, perpetual, non-exclusive, worldwide license to
install and use the Software, on any number of computers, with no registration,
account or payment of any kind.

Permitted use includes personal, devotional, family, academic, congregational
and professional use.

3. PERMITTED REDISTRIBUTION

You may copy the Software's installer or portable version and give it to other
people, provided that all three of the following conditions are met:

  a) you pass it on unmodified, exactly as published by the Licensor;
  b) you charge nothing for the Software, and you do not use it as the object
     or pretext for a charge, including its delivery, installation or support
     when what is actually being charged for is access to the Software.
     Nothing here stops someone who provides their own service from charging
     for their time, provided the Software itself is delivered free and
     without condition; and
  c) this agreement travels with the copy.

This expressly covers copying it to a USB drive, handing it to an acquaintance
or to a congregation on a device, and installing it on other people's computers
free of charge.

4. RESTRICTIONS

Except to the extent that applicable law expressly permits it notwithstanding
this restriction, you may not:

  a) sell, rent, lease, lend for a fee or sublicense the Software, or charge any
     amount whose object is access to the Software, under any label or
     concept;
  b) distribute it as part of a paid product or service, or include it in any
     bundle that is sold;
  c) modify, adapt, translate or create derivative works of the Software;
  d) decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the Software, or attempt to
     obtain its source code by any means. This restriction does not extend to
     extracting the public-domain content bundled with the Software, which
     section 6(a) expressly authorises;
  e) remove, obscure or alter any authorship, license or trademark notices
     contained in the Software.

5. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

The Software is licensed, not sold. The Licensor retains ownership of the code,
the interface design and the other original resources of the Software, together
with all rights not expressly granted in this agreement.

This agreement grants you a right of use; it does not transfer ownership of the
Software or any part of it.

6. BUNDLED CONTENT: WHAT THE LICENSOR DOES NOT OWN

The Software ships with biblical texts and historical works that are NOT the
Licensor's work and over which the Licensor claims no rights.

  a) Public domain texts. The two bundled Bibles (the King James Version and the
     1909 Reina-Valera) and those historical texts whose original and whose
     translation are in the public domain by age are delivered as exactly that:
     public domain work. You may extract them from the Software, copy them and
     reuse them freely, without asking the Licensor for permission and without
     this agreement standing in your way.

  b) Third-party translations. Some of the historical creeds and confessions
     that accompany the Software are reproduced in modern translations whose
     rights belong to their translators or publishers. They are included with
     full credit to their origin and without altering their text. When it has
     been necessary to correct a typographical erratum in a Scripture
     reference from the source edition, the correction is expressly declared
     in that module's record. This agreement grants you
     NO rights over those translations: what you may do with them is up to their
     rights holders, not up to the Licensor of REFORMAMINI.

Each of these texts carries a record, visible inside the Software under module
management, stating its exact source, its translator where it has one, its
publisher and its rights status.

7. USER MODULES AND FILES

The modules, books, documents and files you import into the Software remain
yours, or belong to whoever owns them. Obtaining and using them lawfully is your
responsibility and not the Licensor's.

The Software opens those files read-only: it never modifies or rewrites them.
The Software also does not decrypt protected modules or circumvent any technical
protection measure.

Your notes, highlights, bookmarks and preferences are yours, are stored on your
own computer, and you may take them away or delete them whenever you wish.

8. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Software incorporates third-party code libraries and typefaces, distributed
under their own licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, the SIL Open Font License and other
permissive licenses). Those licenses
continue to apply to those components and are not altered by this agreement.

The full text of those licenses is delivered with the Software and can be read
under Settings, About, Third-party notices.

9. PRIVACY AND ABSENCE OF TELEMETRY

The Software does not collect, does not store on anyone else's servers and does
not transmit any information about you or about your use of the Software,
except for the update check described below. There is no analytics, there are
no user identifiers, there is no advertising and there are no profiles.

All your data (notes, highlights, bookmarks, modules and preferences) lives
exclusively on your own computer.

The Software's only use of the network is the optional check for whether a newer
version exists. In that check the Software sends the installed version and, as
with any internet connection, your IP address is logged by the server it
contacts. No other data is sent, and in particular nothing about your notes,
your modules or your use of the Software is sent. That check can be turned off,
and with it off the Software makes no network connection at all.

10. NO WARRANTY

The Software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including without limitation the warranties of merchantability, fitness
for a particular purpose and non-infringement.

The Licensor does not warrant that the Software will run uninterrupted or
error-free, that it will be compatible with any file or module you wish to open,
or that the results of its use will be accurate or complete.

11. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Licensor shall not be
liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages
arising out of the use of or inability to use the Software, including loss of
data, loss of profits or business interruption, even if advised of the
possibility of such damages.

The Software is free of charge. You are responsible for keeping backups of your
own data.

12. TERMINATION

This agreement terminates automatically if you breach any of its conditions.
Upon termination you must stop using the Software and uninstall it.

You may terminate this agreement at any time by uninstalling the Software. Your
personal data remains on your computer and belongs to you; termination neither
obliges you to delete it nor entitles the Licensor to access it.

Sections 5, 10 and 11 survive termination.

13. TRADEMARK, GOVERNING LAW AND CONTACT

The name "REFORMAMINI" and the logo are trademarks of the Licensor
and are not licensed with the Software. The redistribution permission in section 3 does not
authorise you to use the name or the logo to identify products, services or
versions other than those published by the Licensor.

This agreement is governed by the laws of the United Mexican States. For any
dispute arising from this agreement, the parties expressly submit to the courts
of Mexico City, United Mexican States, waiving any other
venue that might apply to them by reason of their present or future domicile.

"e-Sword" is a trademark of its respective owner. REFORMAMINI reads modules in the
format that program uses, but is not affiliated with it, does not carry its
endorsement or sponsorship, and does not include or use its code.

If any clause of this agreement is held invalid or unenforceable, the remaining
clauses shall remain in full force.

